
TOON 3.0

  Open .toon files or use --input-format toon for standard input. TOON is shown using the
  document view. Searches use normalized JSON text.

  yt                  Copy the complete focused value as canonical TOON.
  pt                  Print the complete focused value as canonical TOON.
  :write file          Write the active root as standard TOON to a new file.
  :w file              Short form of :write.
  :write-toon file     Explicit TOON; :wt is the short form.
  :write-json file     Pretty JSON; :wj is the short form.
  :write-yaml file     YAML document stream; :wy is the short form.
  :write-ndjson file   Compact JSON lines; :write-jsonl and :wn are equivalent.
  :write-sexp file     S-expression output; :ws is the short form (only with sexp).

  Add ! to any available command token to create or replace a file
  (:write!, :w!, :write-toon!, :wt!, :write-json!, :wj!,
  :write-yaml!, :wy!, :write-ndjson!, :write-jsonl!, :wn!,
  and, with sexp, :write-sexp! and :ws!). Without ! existing files are
  not overwritten. The required filename is literal: :write report
  creates "report", not "report.toon"; extensions never select formats.
  Every active root is encoded before opening the file. Encoding errors
  leave it unchanged, but I/O errors after opening can leave partial bytes;
  ! does not guarantee atomic replacement.

  Whole-document writes use all active roots, including filtered subtrees,
  never just the focused value or screen annotations; :. resets the filter.
  TOON output requires exactly one root, string keys, finite JSON numbers,
  and at most 256 nested containers. Decimal precision may be lost;
  duplicate keys keep the last value. yt and pt can select one subtree.
  JSON emits two-space pretty values with final LF per root and no array
  wrapper. YAML starts each document with --- and ends it with LF.
  NDJSON/JSONL emits one compact JSON value and LF per root; arrays stay
  single array records. Optional sexp is unavailable in default builds.

  Migration: :write/:w now use TOON; use :write-json/:wj for former JSON
  writes. Removed :writetoon and :writesexp names are replaced by
  :write-toon and feature-gated :write-sexp; :wt and optional :ws remain.
  CLI input/output selectors still accept only toon, json, yaml.
  Non-terminal output parses and re-encodes TOON input; it does not pass through unchanged.

  toon-spec: 3.0. TOON 4.x syntax is not supported.
